  scene-render.xsd: c068e48a36b605a682920da33eeb6b33aaee397f7c7b9a9f7276c607fd918218
  scene-render.sch: 89b3e6de9215ac907792058ae442c2280a35deae330f4bba5f8e7e73aa572b6d
  capabilities-1.schema.json: 6cb35c8ec6d37df32c9a0ad12eb33332d2abe4f11ac6000a9311d9891ec2e8b3

The XSD and Schematron retain the cinematic extensions below; they are not byte-identical
to the upstream files. The capability JSON Schema is vendored unchanged. Local XML filenames
retain 1.1 for tooling compatibility. SREP 57 generated markers, SREP 59 reference checks
and SREP 63 conditional capability entries are implemented. The former pending SREPs
16, 17, 18, 19, 21 and 26 are implemented; PDF resolution requires the pdf build feature.

Added here, not in sr-core 1.3.0 (SREP 0 of this repository, the cinematic proposal, srep-0000-cinematic-impact.md):
the elements blackHole and accretionDisk (blackHoleType, accretionDiskType; rules BH1 to BH8), camera/@geodesics,
fracture/@source, fracture/@minImpulse and fracture/@energyFraction (rules FRX5 to FRX7), ocean/@density, crater/@mantle,
crater/@bulking and crater/@repose (rules CRT10 to CRT12), and pyro/@follow, @followMargin and @followLoss (rules PYRO9 to
PYRO11); the
rest of the cinematic families (OCN, P3D, CRT, PYC, PYRO, VOL, FRX, MSQ, GEO) is in sr-core 1.3.0 as released. A
release of sr-core that takes these in replaces them; until then a vendoring keeps them (the merge of
2026-10-06 was done by component: every top-level type, group and pattern that sr-core changed since the previous
vendoring is theirs, every one that only this repository changed is ours, and nothing was changed by both).

Local addition ahead of an sr-core release: document version 1.6 (scene/@version gains "1.6"; sr_model::SCHEMA_VERSION
is "1.6"), with the implemented extensions below. A 1.6 document holding 1.5 content validates and renders as the
same document at 1.5. The capability manifest still names the vendored release 1.5.0. A vendoring of sr-core 1.6.0 replaces this.

Added here ahead of an sr-core release: SREP 67 (accepted 2026-10-09). This covers compute, iterate and tonemap
(computeType, densityTonemapType, iterateType), the effect types error-diffusion and segmented-sort with their attributes,
and the Schematron pattern p-srep67 (V13, ITR1, ITR2, SRT1). Three local differences from the SREP's text exist because
of the model generator of sr-model:
- computeType's content is a choice instead of the sequence (param*, tonemap?, behaviour*), with CMP13 keeping one
  tonemap at most;
- the union of tonemap/@reference is named densityReferenceType;
- its keyword is named densityReferenceKeyword.
Every document valid under the SREP is valid here.
Added here ahead of an sr-core release: SREP 68 (accepted 2026-10-09), effectType/@stepsPerFrame and @prewarm, and the
Schematron pattern p-srep68 with STP1, with the syntax of srep/srep-0068.md in sr-core branch srep/drafts-2026-10. The
pattern includes shader effects and program[@mode='step'] (SREP 69). A vendoring of the sr-core release that
contains SREP 68 replaces these.
Unverified for SREP 67 in this engine:
- Real-GPU carry is unverified, because there is no discrete GPU we may use. The two-word 64-bit cells are tested on
  llvmpipe only, in CI and on the prod VM (raster_effects::srep67_compute).
- The error-diffusion kernel weights are checked against the SREP's table and against the commonly republished values,
  not against the original publications, which could not be read from here.

Additional local extensions accepted on 2026-10-09:
- SREPs 66 and 69: build-time and stepping WebAssembly programs, with V12, PRG1 to PRG3 and program diagnostics.
- SREP 70: parametric paths, surfaces and heightfields, with V14, PAR1 and PAR2.
- SREP 72: shader content rectangles, supersampling, edge blending and float32 working textures.
- SREP 73: flock/@orientToVelocity and the INERT-I16 diagnostic for streak flocks.
- SREP 75 (draft, sr-core branch srep/drafts-2026-10): the fractal asset (fractalAssetType, in assetsType) and the
  Schematron pattern p-srep75 (V16, FRC1), with the syntax of srep/srep-0075.md. The model generator of sr-model gains
  the builtin xs:decimal, kept as its exact text. libxml2 (the oracle) refuses an xs:decimal of more than 24 digits, so
  the SREP's kit documents, whose centres have 33, do not validate there; the corpus keeps to 24.
